.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH shiftpaper-slideshow 1  shiftpaper 
.SH NAME
shiftpaper\-slideshow \- Bake several images and show them in turn
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBshiftpaper slideshow\fR [\fB\-i\fR|\fB\-\-interval\fR] [\fB\-s\fR|\fB\-\-shuffle\fR] [\fB\-\-stop\fR] [\fB\-m\fR|\fB\-\-model\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] [\fIINPUTS\fR] 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Bake several images and show them in turn.
.PP
Bakes each image like `set` does, then lists them in config.toml\*(Aqs [slideshow]. A folder adds the images directly inside it, in name order. A running daemon starts the slideshow straight away. \-\-stop, or `set`, goes back to a single wallpaper.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-i\fR, \fB\-\-interval\fR \fI<INTERVAL>\fR [default: 10m]
How long each image shows for, like 90s, 10m or 1h
.TP
\fB\-s\fR, \fB\-\-shuffle\fR
Show the images in a random order, different each time round
.TP
\fB\-\-stop\fR
Stop the slideshow, keeping the image it\*(Aqs showing
.TP
\fB\-m\fR, \fB\-\-model\fR \fI<MODEL>\fR
The ONNX depth model to bake with. Defaults to $SHIFTPAPER_MODEL, then the one in config.toml
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.TP
[\fIINPUTS\fR]
Source images (jpeg, png, or webp), or folders of them
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
shiftpaper slideshow ~/Pictures/walls             Each image for 10 minutes
shiftpaper slideshow a.jpg b.jpg c.jpg \-i 1h      Three images, an hour each
shiftpaper slideshow ~/Pictures/walls \-\-shuffle   In a random order
shiftpaper slideshow \-\-stop                       Keep the current image
.fi
.SH "SEE ALSO"
shiftpaper(1)
.PP
The docs: https://github.com/CPritch/shiftpaper/tree/main/docs
